class:: LiveParam
summary:: A pattern that evaluates a function once per event (live value)
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/LiveStream, Classes/Pfunc, Classes/Vlive, Guides/VisualServer

description::

A link::Classes/Pattern:: whose value is code::func.value(inval):: re-evaluated each event. Timing is controlled entirely by the host link::Classes/Pbind::'s code::\dur:: — code::LiveParam:: never waits internally (an internal wait would be yielded as a parameter value and corrupt the stream). Extra code::*new:: arguments are accepted and ignored for backward compatibility.

Functionally similar to link::Classes/Pfunc::; provided for readable live-input pattern code. link::Classes/LiveStream:: is an alias subclass.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
argument:: func
A link::Classes/Function:: returning the value for this event.
argument:: ... ignored
Accepted and ignored (e.g. legacy code::lag::/code::dur:: args).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: embedInStream
Yields code::func.value(inval):: forever (one value per pulled event).
argument:: inval

EXAMPLES::

code::
~imu = (x: 0);
Routine({ loop { ~imu.x = 1.0.rand2; 0.1.wait } }).play;

Vbind(\instrument, \circle,
    \x, LiveParam({ ~imu.x }),
    \dur, 0.2, \view, \demo
).vplay;
::
